# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event kael_warm_enough
# en: Warm Enough
title [5fcb64] = 够暖了
# en: Kael sits down beside you on the cold bench outside the library. {~Frost creeps from his sleeves onto the stone.|Your tea steams; his breath doesn't.} He holds his bare hands near your mug, not quite touching it, the way you'd hold them near a fire you weren't sure you were allowed to use.
text [f2311f] = 凯尔在图书馆外冰冷的长凳上挨着你坐下。{~霜从他的袖口爬到石头上。|你的茶冒着热气，他呼出的气却没有。}他把光着的双手凑近你的杯子，没有真正碰到，就像人把手凑近一堆不确定自己能不能用的火。
# en: Two students on a cold stone bench under a lamp, one with frost on his sleeves holding his bare hands near the other's mug of tea.
scene [502b9d] = 灯下冰冷的石凳上坐着两个学生，一个袖子上结着霜，把光着的双手凑近另一个人的茶杯。
# en: Wrap his hands round the mug
opt.left.label [748f2b] = 让他的手捧住杯子
# en: {~You fold his fingers round the mug, your hands over his. The tea goes cold in a minute. He doesn't let go. "Warm enough," he says, as if it's a thing he's never said.|You give him the mug and keep your hands on his. Your fingers ache with cold. His, slowly, don't. "Warm enough," he says, testing the words.}
opt.left.say.1 [45625e] = {~你把他的手指拢在杯子上，你的手覆在他手上。一分钟后茶就凉了。他没有松手。“够暖了。”他说，好像这句话他从没说过。|你把杯子给他，手留在他手上。你的手指冻得发疼。他的手指，慢慢地，不疼了。“够暖了。”他说，试着念这几个字。}
# en: Fetch him a second cup
opt.right.label [1598b6] = 再给他端一杯
# en: {~You bring him a cup of his own. It freezes at the rim. He drinks it anyway, solemnly, as if it were a ceremony.|You fetch him a cup from the kitchens. He holds it like something alive. "Nobody brings me hot things," he says. "They assume."}
opt.right.say.1 [d8e9b9] = {~你给他端来一杯他自己的。杯沿结了冰。他还是喝了，郑重其事，像在行一场仪式。|你从厨房给他端来一杯。他捧着它，像捧着一个活物。“从没人给我端热东西，”他说，“他们都以为。”}

@event kael_frost_drawings
# en: Frost Drawings
title [f0db48] = 霜画
# en: The window by your seat in the lecture tower is frosted over, in a lecture hall that's too warm. Looked at closely, the frost-ferns make a face. Yours. Kael, two rows back, has gone very red, which on him is a faint pink.
text [77868c] = 讲堂塔里你座位旁的窗子结了霜，可这间教室明明太热了。凑近细看，那些霜蕨拼成了一张脸。是你的脸。坐在后面两排的凯尔脸红透了——在他脸上，那只是一层淡淡的粉。
# en: A tall classroom window covered in delicate frost-ferns that, looked at closely, make the shape of a face; a pale boy wiping at it with his sleeve.
scene [76ebc1] = 一扇高大的教室窗户上覆满了精致的霜蕨，凑近看是一张脸的形状；一个苍白的男孩正用袖子擦它。
# en: Breathe on the glass and draw one back
opt.left.label [4b3de8] = 呵气在玻璃上回画一张
# en: You breathe on the glass and draw, badly, a boy in a fur coat with a speech bubble that says "...". By the end of the lecture the frost has added a smile to your drawing. Neither of you mentions it afterwards.
opt.left.say.1 [a9f754] = 你在玻璃上呵了口气，歪歪扭扭地画了个穿毛皮大衣的男孩，旁边一个对话框写着“……”。下课时，霜给你的画添了一个笑容。之后你们谁都没提起。
# en: Let him wipe it off
opt.right.label [6251d5] = 让他擦掉
# en: He leans over and wipes it away with his sleeve, mortified. "It does that," he says. "When I'm not paying attention." He paid attention to the rest of the lecture very hard.
opt.right.say.1 [20f64e] = 他探过身用袖子把它擦掉，窘得要命。“它会这样，”他说，“在我不留神的时候。”后半节课他非常非常留神。

@event kael_until_the_thaw
# en: Until the Thaw
title [5afadc] = 等到解冻
# en: At the foot of your staircase, Kael stops. "In the North we don't say goodbye," he says. "It's unlucky. You say 'until the thaw', and touch foreheads, so the cold knows you're coming back." He hasn't said it to anyone here. He's waiting to see if you'll laugh.
text [c237db] = 在你的楼梯口，凯尔停下脚步。“在北境我们不说再见，”他说，“不吉利。要说‘等到解冻’，再碰一下额头，好让寒冷知道你会回来。”在这里他还没对任何人说过。他在等着看你会不会笑。
# en: Two students parting at the foot of a spiral staircase at night, one of them touching his forehead briefly to the other's.
scene [8be6cc] = 夜里，两个学生在螺旋楼梯脚下道别，其中一个把额头轻轻抵在另一个人的额头上。
# en: Touch foreheads
opt.left.label [167ea9] = 碰一下额头
# en: You bend your head to his. His forehead is cold as a windowpane. "Until the thaw," you say. He stands there after you've gone up. You can hear him not moving.
opt.left.say.1 [167df8] = 你低下头抵住他的额头。他的额头凉得像一块窗玻璃。“等到解冻。”你说。你上楼之后他还站在那里。你听得见他一动不动。
# en: Say it back, carefully
opt.right.label [0d9e4f] = 小心地回他一句
# en: "Until the thaw," you say, getting the vowels wrong. He corrects them, gently, three times, until you sound like you were born to it. He looks absurdly pleased.
opt.right.say.1 [d638ba] = “等到解冻。”你说，元音念错了。他温和地纠正了三遍，直到你说得像土生土长的北境人。他看上去高兴得有点过分。

@event kael_bakery_window
# en: Wanting
title [398169] = 想要
# en: You find Kael standing outside the bakery window in the village, looking at the iced buns. He's been there, by the {season == "winter": snow on his shoulders|rain on his collar}, a while. "I'm not hungry," he says, before you ask. He doesn't move.
text [4e9a5b] = 你发现凯尔站在镇上面包房的橱窗外，看着那些糖霜小圆面包。看他{season == "winter": 肩上的雪|领口的雨}，已经站了好一会儿了。“我不饿。”没等你问他就说。他没有挪步。
# en: A pale boy standing outside a village bakery window in the cold, looking at a tray of iced buns, hands in his pockets.
scene [108d53] = 寒风里，一个苍白的男孩双手插兜站在镇上面包房的橱窗外，看着一盘糖霜小圆面包。
# en: Buy him one
opt.left.label [4208f1] = 给他买一个
# en: {~You buy two. He holds his like an unexploded charm. "I wasn't going to," he says. "We weren't — I wasn't supposed to want things." Then he eats it in four bites and looks at you as if you've done something dangerous.|You put a bun in his hands. He looks at it, and at you, and says nothing for a long time. Then: "Thank you for not asking." He eats it slowly, as if someone might take it.}
opt.left.say.1 [d26438] = {~你买了两个。他捧着自己那个，像捧着一枚没爆的符咒。“我本来没打算……”他说，“我们不——我不该想要东西的。”然后他四口吃完，看着你，好像你做了件危险的事。|你把一个面包放进他手里。他看看面包，又看看你，很久没说话。然后：“谢谢你没问。”他吃得很慢，好像会有人来抢。}
# en: Ask which one he'd pick
opt.right.label [5ec6fe] = 问他会挑哪个
# en: {~"The one with the cherry," he says, at once, and then looks shocked at himself. You don't buy it. You just let him have said it, which seems to matter more.|He thinks about it seriously. "None," he says. "All of them." Then, quietly: "Is that allowed?" You tell him it is.}
opt.right.say.1 [6f27a7] = {~“带樱桃的那个。”他立刻说，然后被自己吓了一跳。你没买。你只是让他把这句话说出口，这似乎更要紧。|他认真地想了想。“一个都不要，”他说，“全都要。”然后，很轻地：“可以吗？”你告诉他可以。}

@event kael_lets_himself_want
# en: One Thing a Month
title [853bba] = 每月一件事
# en: Kael has a practice now: once a month, he tells you one thing he wants, out loud. {~This month he's been working up to it for days.|He has it ready. He's written it down so he won't back out.} "I want," he says, and stops, and starts again. "I want to see the sea. With you. Not for a reason."
text [0dae8b] = 凯尔现在有个练习：每个月，他把一件自己想要的东西说出声告诉你。{~这个月他已经酝酿了好几天。|他准备好了。还写了下来，免得临阵退缩。}“我想要，”他说，停住，又重新开口，“我想去看海。和你一起。不为什么。”
# en: A boy and his partner on the castle roof at dusk, him counting something on his cold fingers, very seriously.
scene [c7d2ba] = 黄昏时的城堡屋顶上，一个男孩和他的恋人，他非常认真地掰着冰冷的手指数着什么。
# en: "Then we'll go."
opt.left.label [1057eb] = “那我们就去。”
# en: {~"Just like that?" he says. "Just like that," you say. He laughs, out loud, and frost blooms on every slate of the roof at once.|He nods slowly, as if you've signed something. "Next month," he says, "I'll want something bigger." You find you're looking forward to it.}
opt.left.say.1 [a85ca0] = {~“就这样？”他说。“就这样。”你说。他笑出了声，屋顶上每一片石板一下子都开满了霜花。|他慢慢点头，好像你签了什么约。“下个月，”他说，“我要想要一个更大的。”你发现自己很期待。}
# en: Tell him one of yours
opt.right.label [f437a1] = 告诉他你想要的
# en: {~You tell him something you want. He listens like it's a lesson, and then says, "Yes. That too. I want that for you," and seems surprised that he can.|You trade wants with him until the stars come out. His are small and precise. Yours make him laugh. It's the best lesson either of you has had.}
opt.right.say.1 [d8c9c9] = {~你告诉他一件你想要的东西。他听得像在上课，然后说：“好。这个也要。我想让你得到它。”他似乎惊讶于自己能这样想。|你们交换着各自想要的东西，直到星星出来。他的都很小，很精确。你的逗得他直笑。这是你们俩上过最好的一课。}

@event kael_dont_protect_me
# en: Don't Protect Me
title [e960b8] = 别护着我
# en: An older student says something sharp to you in the corridor, and the floor under his boots freezes solid. He goes down hard. Kael steps between you, frost in the air around him. "Where I'm from," he says, very quietly, "you guard what's yours."
text [6bd28d] = 一个高年级生在走廊里对你说了句刻薄话，他靴子下的地板立刻冻得结结实实。他重重摔倒。凯尔挡到你们中间，周身的空气都结了霜。“在我长大的地方，”他非常轻地说，“你得守住属于你的东西。”
# en: A corridor floor glazed with ice around another student's boots, a pale boy standing between them and his partner, frost in the air.
scene [f740d4] = 走廊地面在另一个学生的靴子周围结了一层亮冰，一个苍白的男孩站在那人和他的恋人之间，空气里飘着霜。
# en: "I'm not yours to guard."
opt.left.label [e10093] = “我不归你守。”
# en: The frost stops. He stares at you. "I didn't — " he says, and then, slowly, "No. You're not." He helps the other boy up himself. Later he says, "Tell me when I do it again," and you do, twice, and then he stops.
opt.left.say.1 [519022] = 霜停了。他盯着你。“我不是——”他说，然后慢慢地：“对。你不归我守。”他亲手把那个男孩扶了起来。后来他说：“我再这样就告诉我。”你说了两次，之后他就不再这样了。
# en: Let him, this once
opt.right.label [20292d] = 这一次，由他去
# en: The corridor clears around you both. People step aside for you for a week. Kael walks you to every lesson, and you start to understand that he doesn't know another way to say it.
opt.right.say.1 [783589] = 你们俩周围的走廊空了。整整一周，人们都给你让路。凯尔每节课都陪你走过去，你渐渐明白，他不知道还能用别的什么方式来表达。

@event kael_proud_of_you
# en: Proud of You
title [18f975] = 为你骄傲
# en: Kael has done something hard, a practical he wasn't sure he'd pass, and passed it well. There's a letter from home on his bed. He hasn't opened it. "It won't say it," he tells you. "It never does. I don't know why I keep hoping."
text [052e37] = 凯尔做成了一件难事：一场他没把握能过的实践考，他考得很好。他床上放着一封家信，还没拆。“它不会说的，”他告诉你，“从来不说。我不知道自己为什么还抱着希望。”
# en: A pale boy on the edge of a bed with an unopened letter in Northern script, his partner sitting down beside him.
scene [90379f] = 一个苍白的男孩坐在床沿，手里一封北境字迹的信没有拆开，他的恋人在他身边坐下。
# en: Say it for her
opt.left.label [2b0ddd] = 替她说出来
# en: "I'm proud of you," you say. He looks at you the way he did his first night here, at a piece of bread nobody had to offer. Then he puts the letter in a drawer, unopened, and doesn't take it out again.
opt.left.say.1 [6a4d6a] = “我为你骄傲。”你说。他看着你的样子，就像他来的第一晚看着那块没人非给不可的面包。然后他把信放进抽屉，没拆，再也没拿出来过。
# en: "I'm proud of you," you say. He doesn't move for a long time. Then he puts the letter in a drawer, unopened, and asks you to say it again, just once, so he'll know he didn't imagine it.
opt.left.say.2 [a117e4] = “我为你骄傲。”你说。他很久没有动。然后他把信放进抽屉，没拆，请你再说一遍，就一遍，好让他知道不是自己想象出来的。
# en: Open it together
opt.right.label [b08f88] = 一起拆开
# en: You open it together. It's about the weather and his uncle's knee. At the bottom, after the signature, in a different, hurried hand: "Well done." He reads it eleven times. It's more than he's ever had.
opt.right.say.1 [5b6ec7] = 你们一起拆开。信里说的是天气和他叔叔的膝盖。在最底下，署名之后，换了一种匆忙的笔迹：“做得好。”他读了十一遍。这比他以往得到的都多。

@event kael_ex
# en: Frost Recedes
title [317cae] = 霜退
# en: You notice it on a cold morning: the corridor windows are frosted over, every one, except the panes you walk past. Kael is at the far end. When he sees you, the frost on his side of the hall draws back, carefully, the way you'd step out of someone's road.
text [931623] = 一个寒冷的早晨你注意到了：走廊的窗子全都结了霜，唯独你经过的那几块玻璃没有。凯尔在走廊尽头。看见你时，他那一侧的霜小心翼翼地退开了，就像人给别人让路。
# en: A long corridor of tall windows, frost on every pane except the ones nearest a student walking past alone.
scene [269d68] = 一条长长的走廊排着高窗，每一块玻璃都结着霜，只有一个独自走过的学生身旁那几块没有。
# en: Walk on
opt.left.label [383259] = 继续走
# en: You walk on. The frost closes behind you. It's a kindness, you think, of a kind: he's keeping out of your way so precisely that it must take all his attention.
opt.left.say.1 [460841] = 你继续往前走。霜在你身后合拢。你想，这也算一种体贴：他避开你避得这样精确，一定耗尽了他全部的注意力。
# en: Walk up to him
opt.right.label [d512ec] = 走到他面前
# en: You say his name. He flinches, and then doesn't. "Until the thaw?" you ask, and he almost smiles. "Until the thaw," he says. The frost comes back across the windows, slowly, all of them, yours too.
opt.right.say.1 [a9f338] = 你叫他的名字。他瑟缩了一下，又没有。“等到解冻？”你问。他几乎笑了。“等到解冻。”他说。霜慢慢地爬回所有窗子上，你身旁的也一样。
# en: "Don't," he says, very gently. "Please. I'm not good at this part. I wasn't taught it." He goes. The windows stay clear where you stand.
opt.right.say.2 [89c09e] = “别，”他非常温和地说，“求你了。这部分我做不好。没人教过我。”他走了。你站着的地方，窗子依然透亮。

@event kael_gift_given
# en: A Snowflake Under Glass
title [57be9e] = 玻璃罩里的雪花
# en: There's a parcel in your pigeonhole, cold to the touch. Inside, wrapped in a scrap of fur, is a tiny glass dome with a single snowflake in it. It hasn't melted. A note in sharp Northern handwriting: "It won't. I asked it not to."
text [ee4555] = 你的信格里有个包裹，摸上去冰凉。里面裹着一块毛皮，毛皮里是一个小小的玻璃罩，罩着一片雪花。它没有融化。一张字条，笔迹是锋利的北境字体：“它不会化的。我请它别化。”
# en: A tiny glass dome in a student's palm, a single perfect snowflake inside it that has not melted.
scene [3cb672] = 一个学生的掌心里托着一个小玻璃罩，里面一片完美的雪花，没有融化。
# en: Keep it on your windowsill
opt.left.label [99b65b] = 摆在窗台上
# en: It catches the light every morning. On the hottest day of the year you check it, worried. The snowflake is still there, perfect. So, you think, is he: careful, and very stubborn about what lasts.
opt.left.say.1 [edb04f] = 每天早上它都映着光。一年里最热的那天，你担心地去看。雪花还在，完好无缺。你想，他也是这样：小心翼翼，又对什么该长久这件事非常固执。
# en: Give him something warm back
opt.right.label [d2eec6] = 回送他点暖和的
# en: You find him a scarf, thick and red and absurd. He wears it at once, even indoors. Frost forms on it and he picks it off, flake by flake, as if he's protecting it.
opt.right.say.1 [7b10bc] = 你给他找了一条围巾，又厚又红，滑稽极了。他当场就围上了，在屋里也不摘。围巾上结了霜，他一片一片地摘掉，好像在保护它。

@event nessa_the_one_phrase
# en: The One Phrase
title [1c14a5] = 那一句话
# en: You tell Nessa something about your day and her quill writes it down. {~It always does.|You're used to it by now.} "Sorry," she says. "It takes everything. There's one phrase that stops it, you know. I've never used it." She doesn't say what it is. She looks at you as if she's deciding.
text [f0280b] = 你跟内莎说起你这一天，她的羽毛笔把它记了下来。{~它总是这样。|你已经习惯了。}“抱歉，”她说，“它什么都记。你知道吗，有一句话能让它停下。我从来没用过。”她没说是哪句。她看着你，像在做决定。
# en: A girl at a cluttered desk with a self-writing quill scratching beside her, glaring at it, while another student leans on the desk.
scene [74d756] = 一个女孩坐在杂乱的书桌前，一支自动书写的羽毛笔在她身旁沙沙作响，她瞪着它，另一个学生倚在桌边。
# en: Don't ask; let her decide
opt.left.label [3f66a5] = 不问，让她自己决定
# en: {~You say nothing. She keeps looking, and the quill keeps writing, and then she tells you what the phrase is, which is not the same as using it. "Off the record," she says. "Not yet." The quill writes that down too.|You wait. "Off the record," she says at last, as a definition, not a command. "That's the phrase. Someday I'll say it to somebody." The quill underlines "someday" twice.}
opt.left.say.1 [e6301c] = {~你什么都没说。她一直看着你，羽毛笔一直在写，然后她告诉了你那句话是什么——告诉你，和真正对它说，不是一回事。“不作记录，”她说，“还不到时候。”羽毛笔把这句也记下了。|你等着。“不作记录，”她终于说，像在下定义，而不是在下命令，“就是这句话。总有一天我会对某个人说。”羽毛笔在“总有一天”下面画了两道线。}
# en: Guess the phrase
opt.right.label [33207a] = 猜那句话
# en: {~You guess "please stop". The quill writes "PLEASE STOP" in capitals and keeps going. Nessa laughs so hard she has to sit down.|You guess "the end". The quill writes "THE END" and then, to make a point, a sequel. Nessa gives you a mark out of ten. It's a four.}
opt.right.say.1 [12dd59] = {~你猜“请停下”。羽毛笔用大写字母写下“请停下”，然后继续写。内莎笑得不得不坐下。|你猜“全文完”。羽毛笔写下“全文完”，然后为了表明立场，又写了一篇续集。内莎给你打了个分：十分里的四分。}

@event nessa_quill_draft
# en: The Quill's Draft
title [6ad1a4] = 羽毛笔的草稿
# en: There's a draft on Nessa's desk in the quill's handwriting, headed "EXCLUSIVE: THE EDITOR AND THE SOURCE." It's about you. And her. And a great many moonlit walks that never happened. Nessa comes in, sees you reading it, and turns the colour of red ink.
text [4dda1e] = 内莎桌上有一份草稿，是羽毛笔的笔迹，标题是“独家：主编与线人”。写的是你。和她。还有许许多多根本没发生过的月下漫步。内莎走进来，看见你在读，脸红得像红墨水。
# en: A sheet of newsprint on a desk with an over-written headline about two students, a mortified girl snatching for it.
scene [315008] = 桌上一张新闻稿，标题夸张地写着两个学生的事，一个窘迫的女孩伸手去抢。
# en: Hand it back unread
opt.left.label [3ab727] = 不读，还给她
# en: You fold it and hand it back. "I didn't read past the headline," you lie. "It invents things," she says, too fast. "Left alone. It makes up the news." She folds it smaller. She doesn't throw it away.
opt.left.say.1 [38a989] = 你把它折好还给她。“我只看了标题。”你撒谎。“它会编东西，”她说得太快，“没人看着就编。它会编造新闻。”她把纸折得更小。她没扔掉。
# en: Read the best line aloud
opt.right.label [6164c1] = 把最好的一句念出来
# en: You read out "their eyes met over the proofs like two scandals". Nessa puts her face in her hands. "It makes things up," she says, through her fingers. "When I'm not watching it." Then, muffled: "That line's not even good."
opt.right.say.1 [f9e309] = 你念出“他们的目光在校样上相遇，像两桩丑闻”。内莎把脸埋进手里。“它编的，”她从指缝里说，“我不看着它就编。”然后闷闷地：“那句话写得都不好。”

@event nessa_deadline_night
# en: Deadline Night
title [d06cb7] = 截稿夜
# en: The Ledger goes to the printer at midnight and Nessa is three columns short. {~Ink on her face, ink in her hair.|The press is waiting under its dust sheet.} "I don't need help," she says. "I need a miracle, or a typesetter who doesn't sleep."
text [2b17ae] = 《流明纪事报》午夜就要付印，内莎还缺三栏。{~脸上是墨，头发上也是墨。|印刷机在防尘布下等着。}“我不需要帮忙，”她说，“我需要一个奇迹，或者一个不睡觉的排字工。”
# en: A newspaper office at night, proofs everywhere, a girl with ink on her face, a printing press waiting under a dust sheet.
scene [5ec241] = 夜里的报社编辑部，校样到处都是，一个女孩脸上沾着墨，一台印刷机盖着防尘布等在一旁。
# en: Set type until midnight
opt.left.label [112e43] = 陪她排字到午夜
# en: {~You set type with her until your fingers are black. At two minutes to midnight she slots in the last line, and kisses the press, and then, quickly, as if it were the same thing, your cheek.|You read proofs aloud while she sets them. You catch four errors. She catches you yawning, and calls it the fifth. The paper goes out on time.}
opt.left.say.1 [4ff21e] = {~你陪她排字，排到手指发黑。午夜前两分钟，她塞进最后一行，亲了一下印刷机，然后飞快地，好像是同一件事似的，亲了一下你的脸颊。|她排版，你把校样念出来。你挑出四处错误。她抓到你打哈欠，说这算第五处。报纸按时付印了。}
# en: Write the third column yourself
opt.right.label [31465d] = 自己写第三栏
# en: {~You write it in an hour. She cuts a third and calls it "almost good", which from Nessa is a medal. It runs under "Staff".|Your column runs. Nessa edits it so hard it bleeds, and then pins the proof on her wall.}
opt.right.say.1 [a53b7e] = {~你一个钟头就写完了。她删掉三分之一，说“差不多能看”——从内莎嘴里说出来，这是一枚勋章。它署名“本报”刊出。|你的专栏刊出了。内莎改得它鲜血淋漓，然后把校样钉在了她的墙上。}
# en: {~She reads it, says "no", kindly, and writes the column herself in twenty minutes. She keeps your draft anyway.|It's not good. She tells you so, and why, for ten minutes, and you learn more about writing than in a year of essays.}
opt.right.say.2 [375de3] = {~她读完，温和地说了声“不行”，然后二十分钟自己写完了那一栏。你的草稿她还是留着。|写得不好。她告诉你不好，还说了为什么，说了十分钟，你从中学到的写作比一整年的论文都多。}

@event nessa_shared_byline
# en: A Shared Byline
title [bff3c4] = 联合署名
# en: Nessa shows you the proof of next week's lead story. You helped with it, a little: one interview, one fact you checked. Under the headline it says "by Nessa Quill and" — and then your name. "It's accurate," she says, too casually. "I only print what's accurate."
text [3f322e] = 内莎给你看下周头条的校样。你帮过一点忙：一次采访，一个核实过的事实。标题下写着“内莎·奎尔与”——然后是你的名字。“这是准确的，”她说，故作随意，“我只刊登准确的东西。”
# en: A newspaper proof with two names printed side by side under a headline, one student pointing at them, the other pretending not to care.
scene [89447f] = 一张报纸校样，标题下并排印着两个名字，一个学生指着它们，另一个装作不在乎。
# en: Keep your name on it
opt.left.label [7f6068] = 保留你的名字
# en: The story runs with both your names. People stop you in the corridor about it. Nessa cuts the byline out of the proof copy and keeps it in her notebook, where you're not supposed to see.
opt.left.say.1 [b44fb4] = 报道署着你们俩的名字刊出了。人们在走廊里拦住你聊这篇文章。内莎把校样上的署名剪下来，夹在她的笔记本里——你本不该看见的地方。
# en: "It's your story. Take it."
opt.right.label [e07f8a] = “这是你的报道。你署名。”
# en: She looks almost hurt, then very much not. "You're the first person who's ever tried to give me credit back," she says. "Fine. But you're in the acknowledgements. In large type."
opt.right.say.1 [3805d1] = 她看上去几乎受伤了，随即又完全不是。“你是第一个想把功劳还给我的人，”她说，“行。但你得上致谢。大号字。”

@event nessa_corrections_column
# en: Corrections
title [2a1126] = 更正
# en: Every week the Ledger's corrections column has a paragraph only you can read. {~This week: "Correction: last Tuesday we reported the weather as fair. It was, in fact, lovely, for reasons the editor declines to give."|This week: "Correction: the editor did not, as reported, sleep at her desk. She slept on someone's shoulder, which is not a desk."}
text [0f8d75] = 每周，《流明纪事报》的更正栏里都有一段只有你看得懂。{~本周：“更正：上周二本报称天气晴好。实际上是美好，原因主编拒绝透露。”|本周：“更正：主编并未如报道所称在办公桌上睡着。她是靠在某人肩上睡着的，那不是办公桌。”}
# en: A student reading the back page of a school newspaper over breakfast, smiling at a tiny paragraph in the corrections box.
scene [03b18d] = 早餐时，一个学生读着校报的最后一版，对着更正栏里一小段文字微笑。
# en: Write one back
opt.left.label [ce6383] = 回她一条
# en: {~You slip a correction under her door: "Correction: the reader was not 'mildly pleased'. The reader was delighted." It runs the next week, verbatim, in a box with a border.|You send in a correction of the correction. She prints it with a correction of that. It goes on for a month. The rest of the school thinks the Ledger's lost its mind.}
opt.left.say.1 [947c2a] = {~你把一条更正塞到她门下：“更正：读者并非‘略感愉快’。读者是欣喜。”下周它原封不动地刊出了，还加了个带边框的方框。|你寄去一条对更正的更正。她刊出了对那条的更正。来来回回持续了一个月。全校都以为《纪事报》疯了。}
# en: Read it aloud at breakfast
opt.right.label [0c0ce7] = 早餐时念出来
# en: {~You read it aloud. Nobody else understands it. Nessa, three tables away, puts her head down on her toast.|You read it aloud with feeling. Half the table works it out. Nessa runs no corrections the following week, which is its own sort of correction.}
opt.right.say.1 [e0f7cb] = {~你念了出来。没人听得懂。隔着三张桌子的内莎把头埋进了吐司里。|你声情并茂地念了出来。半桌人听懂了。下一周内莎一条更正都没登，这本身也算一种更正。}

@event nessa_not_a_story
# en: Not a Story
title [79b584] = 不是一篇报道
# en: Nessa has written a feature. It's beautiful. It's about you: where you came from, what you told her late at night, what you're afraid of. Names changed. "Nobody would know," she says. "It's the best thing I've ever written."
text [a50478] = 内莎写了一篇特稿。写得很美。写的是你：你从哪里来，深夜里你对她说过的话，你害怕什么。名字都改过了。“没人会知道的，”她说，“这是我写过最好的东西。”
# en: A girl holding out a typed draft to her partner across a desk, eager, the partner not taking it, the quill between them frozen mid-word.
scene [f4dba8] = 一个女孩隔着书桌把一份打好的稿子递给她的恋人，满怀期待，对方没有接，两人之间的羽毛笔停在半个字上。
# en: "I'm not a story."
opt.left.label [8971b7] = “我不是一篇报道。”
# en: She means it kindly; make her hear you.
opt.left.hint [7fdcb8] = 她是好意；让她听见你。
# en: It takes an hour. She argues like an editor; you argue like someone who's been edited. At the end she stops, and looks at the draft, and puts it in the drawer with the quill. "Off the record," she says. "All of it. Always. I'm sorry."
opt.left.say.1 [c98023] = 说了一个钟头。她像编辑一样争，你像被编辑过的人一样争。最后她停下来，看着那份稿子，把它和羽毛笔一起放进了抽屉。“不作记录，”她说，“全部。永远。对不起。”
# en: She doesn't print it. She doesn't understand why, either, and she says so, at length, and you both go to bed angry. In the morning the draft is gone from her desk. You don't know where.
opt.left.say.2 [340450] = 她没登。她也不明白为什么不能登，还滔滔不绝地这么说了，你们俩带着气上了床。第二天早上，草稿从她桌上不见了。你不知道去了哪里。
# en: Let her print it
opt.right.label [24f82f] = 让她登出来
# en: It runs. People cry over it in the refectory. Nobody guesses it's you, quite. Nessa is radiant all week, and you feel, oddly, like a photograph of yourself.
opt.right.say.1 [d53d6b] = 文章刊出了。膳堂里有人读着读着哭了。没人完全猜出是你。内莎一整周容光焕发，而你奇怪地觉得自己像一张自己的照片。

@event nessa_press_breaks
# en: The Press Breaks
title [348b25] = 印刷机坏了
# en: The Ledger's press has cracked down the middle, a hundred years old and done. Nessa is sitting on the floor beside it. "Forty years we haven't missed an issue," she says, very steady. "I'll copy it out by hand. Every copy. I'll chain myself to it if I have to." She isn't joking.
text [8c22be] = 《纪事报》的印刷机从中间裂开了，一百岁了，彻底完了。内莎坐在它旁边的地上。“四十年来我们一期都没落下过，”她说得很平稳，“我会手抄。每一份。必要的话我就把自己锁在它上面。”她不是在开玩笑。
# en: An old iron printing press with a cracked frame, a girl sitting on the floor beside it with her knees drawn up, ink on her hands.
scene [6b9dfc] = 一台机架裂开的旧铁印刷机，一个女孩抱着膝坐在它旁边的地上，手上沾着墨。
# en: Copy it out with her, all night
opt.left.label [0d8f85] = 陪她抄一整夜
# en: You copy out three hundred Ledgers by hand, by candlelight, with half the club. At dawn the last one dries. Nessa falls asleep on the stack, ink on her nose, and the issue goes out on time, every copy in a different hand.
opt.left.say.1 [1f82b0] = 你和半个报社的人一起，借着烛光手抄了三百份《纪事报》。黎明时最后一份晾干了。内莎趴在那摞报纸上睡着了，鼻尖沾着墨。这一期按时发出，每一份的笔迹都不一样。
# en: Find Mir
opt.right.label [4511c6] = 去找米尔
# en: Mir looks at the press for a long minute, says "oh, you poor old thing", and spends three nights with a welding charm. It prints again, louder than before. Nessa hugs Mir so hard their goggles come off.
opt.right.say.1 [55b7f3] = 米尔盯着印刷机看了好一会儿，说了句“哦，可怜的老家伙”，然后拿着焊接咒忙了三个晚上。它又能印了，比以前还响。内莎紧紧抱住米尔，把TA的护目镜都抱掉了。
# en: You don't know anyone who can mend it, so you hire someone from the village. It costs. It prints. Nessa says she'll pay you back; you both know she'll pay you back in column inches.
opt.right.say.2 [a6e36f] = 你不认识能修它的人，就从镇上雇了个师傅。花了钱。它能印了。内莎说她会还你钱；你们俩都知道，她会用专栏篇幅来还。

@event nessa_ex
# en: Retraction
title [ec6898] = 撤回声明
# en: In this week's Ledger, at the very bottom of the back page, in the smallest type the press has: "Retraction. The editor regrets an earlier statement, made off the record, that she was certain. She was not. She is sorry." Nessa is in the doorway, watching you read it.
text [0f1f4d] = 本周的《纪事报》，最后一版的最底下，用印刷机能排出的最小号字写着：“撤回声明。主编对此前一则不作记录的声明表示遗憾——她当时说她很确定。她并不确定。她很抱歉。”内莎站在门口，看着你读。
# en: A tiny boxed paragraph on the back page of a school newspaper, a student reading it alone in a window seat.
scene [06fdee] = 校报最后一版上一个小小的方框段落，一个学生独自坐在窗台上读着它。
# en: Fold the paper and go
opt.left.label [4f92dc] = 折起报纸离开
# en: You fold the Ledger and put it in your bag. You don't look back. Weeks later you find it again, the little paragraph worn soft where you've folded it, over and over.
opt.left.say.1 [38d5fa] = 你把《纪事报》折好放进书包。你没回头。几周后你又翻出它来，那一小段被你折了又折，已经磨软了。
# en: Go and talk to her
opt.right.label [2c043a] = 去和她谈谈
# en: "On the record," you say, "I'd like to be friends." Her quill, at her shoulder, writes it down, and she lets it. "Printed," she says. "No retractions."
opt.right.say.1 [7d63de] = “作记录，”你说，“我想和你做朋友。”她肩头的羽毛笔把这句记了下来，她由着它记。“已付印，”她说，“不撤回。”
# en: She starts to say something, and then her quill starts writing, and she looks at it, and at you, and puts it away. "Not yet," she says. "I'm still drafting."
opt.right.say.2 [5f1724] = 她刚要开口，羽毛笔就开始写了，她看看它，又看看你，把它收了起来。“还不到时候，”她说，“我还在打草稿。”

@event nessa_argument
# en: On the Record
title [6a1830] = 作记录
# en: You and Nessa are arguing about something small, and it's getting less small, and halfway through you realise her quill is taking it down. Verbatim. With stage directions. "Ignore it," she says. "Go on. You were saying I'm 'impossible'?"
text [5dde21] = 你和内莎为一件小事争了起来，事情越吵越不小，吵到一半你才发现她的羽毛笔在记录。一字不差。还带舞台提示。“别管它，”她说，“继续。你刚才说我‘不可理喻’？”
# en: Two students arguing in a corridor, one of them with a notebook out, a quill floating at her shoulder taking it all down.
scene [298aab] = 两个学生在走廊里争吵，其中一个掏出了笔记本，一支羽毛笔悬在她肩头记录着一切。
# en: Make her put the quill away
opt.left.label [086bf7] = 让她把笔收起来
# en: "Not with that thing listening." She glares, and then, astonishingly, puts it in her pocket. The argument dies without an audience. "You're right," she says. "Don't quote me."
opt.left.say.1 [3bd92c] = “那东西听着我可不吵。”她瞪着你，然后，出人意料地，把它收进了口袋。没了听众，争吵自己就熄了。“你说得对，”她说，“别引用我。”
# en: Argue for the record
opt.right.label [fb2aca] = 当着记录吵
# en: You argue it out for the record, both of you playing to the quill, until you're laughing too hard to finish. The transcript is pinned on her wall under "best interview of the year".
opt.right.say.1 [8accc0] = 你们当着记录吵到底，两个人都在冲着羽毛笔表演，最后笑得吵不下去。那份记录被钉在她的墙上，标题是“年度最佳采访”。
# en: You argue for the record. She wins on points, and prints a column the next week about "people who say 'impossible' when they mean 'right'". You aren't named. Everyone knows.
opt.right.say.2 [bddded] = 你们当着记录吵。她以点数取胜，下一周登了篇专栏，讲“那些说‘不可理喻’其实意思是‘你说得对’的人”。没点你的名。大家都知道。
